Dear Friends,

Greetings from the University of Tokyo Indian Students Association. As a President of the association, 

I am pleased to invite you to the exciting seminar , "A culture of Innovation" which is going to be held on Tuesday, October 12th from 17.45, at Medical Library (3F. Room No. 333).

Seminar will be delivered by Prof. Chris Beamount, reknowned corporate leader over 18 years of experience and Professor at University of Tokyo 

and also worked as a Professor for a decade at London School of Business focusing on decision science. 

Participation in the seminar will help us to exchange the ideas and to promote the interaction between all the International students including Japanese students.

 Seminar is focused on the culture of Innovation. 

Details of the event can be found at the website:

http://utisa.org/events-galleries

Hurry up for the registration. 

You are requested to register ( Name, School, Country of origin) latest by 8th October at the following email address :

 rafipharmbio@gmail.com 

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A Culture of Innovation?!
In a country concerned daily about the natural forces of their environment (the big earthquake is long overdue in Tokyo!), the peoples of Japan have established an ordered and harmonious, society where adding value is just as much a part of their DNA as their survival mentality. 
Post-war growth was fuelled by a focus on science and technology as agents of change. However, self evidently the Japanese business model that was the envy of the world in the 1980/90’s has not been replaced in today’s post-bubble era, and Japan remains a fortress to foreigners. 
The new mentality in the ‘land of the setting sun’ still places a primacy on innovation and craftsmanship where newness facilitates self-expression. Paradoxically, in today’s nano-tech and connected world the Japanese demand for ‘freshness’ can provide lessons that travel the world where attention to detail can make the small differences look new.
