Student organizations at the University of Tokyo

Dear all,

 Good morning, this is the administrative office at Todai.

 Here we forward a notification from MINISTRY OF EDUCATION, CULTURE,
 SPORTS, SCIENCE and TECHNOLOGY-JAPAN about the bird flu.
 Please find the attached PDF about the measures against the bird flu
 and share the information with your members.

 (A brief translation of the notification)
 1. Wash hands and gargle after going outside.
 2. Stay away from dead birds.
 3. Inform the school, veterinary surgeon or health administration
 office when you find dead birds.
 4. If you keep birds for a pet, try to keep them inside of the house
 and keep them away from wild birds.
 Try to have a roof to prevent the pets from excreta of wild birds.
 5. Have the right knowledge about the bird flu.
 Please be reminded that the bird flu is a disease only for the birds
 and there will be no circulation of infected chicken and eggs in the
 market.
 If you had the infected chicken and eggs by any accident, you won''t
 catch the flu and it won''t affect your health either.

Thank you for your cooperation and take good care of yourself.
Wish all of you have a healthy new year!

********************************************
