SUMMARY OF WORKSHOP

 

 
[INFORMATION]

This workshop is to improve your disaster imagination
skill of possible upcoming Earthquake Events in Tokyo. The idea is to calibrate
the disaster response of individuals by using a chart named “Meguro-Maki”.
Participant of this workshop will be subjected to a disaster scenario and asked
to note down their immediate response and long term response on Meguro-Maki. It’s
not kind of a passive lecture but active working. It is a very valuable chance
for you to join this event and improve your disaster prevention skill.

 

 

 

[DATE&PLACE]

December 10th 13:00~14:30 
@Univ. of Tokyo
Hongo Campus Faculty of Engineering
Bldg.1 Civil Enginnering Department Seminar room B

December 11th 13:00~14:30 
@Univ. of Tokyo
Hongo Campus Faculty of Engineering
Bldg.1 Civil Enginnering Department Seminar room A

December 12th 13:00~14:30 
@Univ. of Tokyo
Hongo Campus Faculty of Engineering Bldg.1
Civil Enginnering Department Seminar room A

December 13th 17:00~18:30 @Univ. of Tokyo Komaba IIS Campus An block Bldg.
An-401 room 

 

 [TIME NEEDS]

an hour ~ an hour and a half

 

