On behalf of the KAIST students and faculty, we invite your students to our conference PIONEERS 2071: Questioning the Next 50 Years, which is a semi-centennial event of KAIST for undergraduate students all around the world. Please share the poster and invitation letter with your students. 
 
The purpose of the conference is to provide students with the opportunity to explore potential global crises that may happen over the next 50 years and propose possible solutions with policies, technology, and innovative ideas. 
 
Conference Dates: Feb 2–7, 2021 (GMT+9) 
Registration Dates: Dec 14, 2020–Jan 15, 2021 (GMT+9)
 

We will send out notification emails to participants within a few days after the registration closes.
 
* The conference will be held online, in English.
* The total amount of prize of the conference is $10000.
* Please refer to our website (pioneers.kaist.ac.kr), Instagram (@pioneers.2071) and attached files for more information.
* The conference will be held online.
* Please refer to our website (pioneers.kaist.ac.kr) and attached files for more information.
 
Best regards, 
 
KAIST PIONEERS 2071 Planning Committee

